1
00:00:59,193 --> 00:01:04,519
<v Tutor>So you were both given your project assignments for your senior thesis today right?

2
00:01:04,519 --> 00:01:08,406
<v Jane>Yes, and we already have to submit our topics next week!

3
00:01:08,406 --> 00:01:11,476
<v Mark>But how could they give us a grade this soon?

4
00:01:11,476 --> 00:01:15,511
<v Tutor>No, next week’s due date will not be counted towards your final grade.

5
00:01:15,511 --> 00:01:19,586
The teachers are just going to read your topic and give you feedback.

6
00:01:19,586 --> 00:01:24,744
<v Jane>Oh, I see. So first we should come up with our topics, and then what?

7
00:01:24,744 --> 00:01:30,433
<v Tutor>Well, once you know what you want to study, you need to think about how you’ll study it.

8
00:01:30,423 --> 00:01:35,625
You need to decide on your research methods. The methods will be the main part of your paper.

9
00:01:35,625 --> 00:01:37,894
<v Mark>What about the results section?

10
00:01:37,884 --> 00:01:47,537
<v Tutor>Well, I can give you feedback on that, but you will be the one carrying out an experiment and thus will have to produce the results on your own.

11
00:01:47,537 --> 00:01:54,154
What I would like to do today is practise writing research papers before you even begin your reports.

12
00:01:54,154 --> 00:02:02,291
I’ll give you samples of old data from past experience, and you can practice writing results and drawing conclusions.

13
00:02:02,291 --> 00:02:04,299
<v Jane>I think that would be really helpful.

14
00:02:04,299 --> 00:02:10,096
<v Mark>Yeah, it sounds like a lot of extra work, but I’m sure it will make our actual project easier.

15
00:02:10,096 --> 00:02:17,203
<v Tutor>You exactly right. So let’s get started. First, let’s try this simple experiment on fruit flies.

16
00:02:17,203 --> 00:02:27,507
Read the information, and then take 25 minutes to summarise a results and conclusion section. That’s really important - pay attention to the time limit.

17
00:02:27,507 --> 00:02:30,631
<v Jane>OK, does it still have to be 6,000 words?

18
00:02:30,631 --> 00:02:32,569
<v Tutor>No, don’t worry about that

19
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,575
<v Mark>What if we get off topic?

20
00:02:34,575 --> 00:02:41,970
<v Tutor>I wouldn’t worry too much - you will have so much information to write about that it should be easy to stay on topic.

21
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:20,842
<v Jane>But what about other sources?

22
00:03:20,842 --> 00:03:25,697
<v Tutor>Well for this assignment, you can use the one from your textbook.

23
00:03:25,697 --> 00:03:30,746
In your actual paper, you should find old experiments that support your topic.

24
00:03:30,746 --> 00:03:39,040
<v Mark>So do we need to find different types of sources? For instance, should I be conducting lots of interviews to use in my paper?

25
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:44,167
<v Tutor>No, there’s no need to conduct lots of interviews or anything like that.

26
00:03:44,167 --> 00:03:50,769
<v Mark>OK, I’m ready to get started. I’m still a little confused though, on how we should format our paper.

27
00:03:50,769 --> 00:04:00,812
<v Tutor>Don’t worry about it for now, but on your final paper, make sure to pay attention to the format. It should follow the guidelines exactly.

28
00:04:00,802 --> 00:04:05,982
<v Jane>Oh man, I’m starting to understand why they give us all semester to do this.

29
00:04:05,982 --> 00:04:09,898
Are there any other small details like that that we should know about?

30
00:04:09,898 --> 00:04:17,739
<v Tutor>Not a whole lot, make sure you provide two copies - one for your teacher of course, but one for yourself as well.

31
00:04:17,739 --> 00:04:20,568
And of course, you know the due date, right?

32
00:04:20,568 --> 00:04:22,791
<v Mark>Uh, it’s April 11, right?

33
00:04:22,791 --> 00:04:26,809
<v Jane>What? No! It’s May 11. Right?

34
00:04:26,809 --> 00:04:31,302
<v Tutor>Yes. The due date is May 11. Write it down!

35
00:04:31,302 --> 00:04:39,634
<v Mark>Oh wow. Yeah, I need to note it. Also, I’m having trouble finding information on my topic. What if i can’t find enough good sources?

36
00:04:39,634 --> 00:04:45,074
<v Tutor>It’s alright to change your topic. Just make sure to do it before the beginning of April.

37
00:04:45,074 --> 00:04:48,362
<v Mark>Oh really? Wow, I’m definitely going to change it then.

38
00:04:48,362 --> 00:04:53,603
<v Tutor>Just make sure to write a note to your teacher letting him or her know.

39
00:04:53,603 --> 00:05:01,380
<v Jane>Okay. So getting back to writing this sample paper, where do we start? Should I just explain the experiment and what happened?

40
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:08,492
<v Tutor>Well, you need to start with your hypothesis - what you think will happen - and then describe your procedure.

41
00:05:08,492 --> 00:05:12,209
Then you can write up the results and your conclusions.

42
00:05:12,209 --> 00:05:17,161
<v Jane>Oh boy, I don’t know if I can handle any more instructions…